WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:21.240
The school supply framework has three anchors: diastolic time, coronary patency and arterial oxygen content. Left ventricular coronary perfusion occurs predominantly during diastole, when compression of vessels by contracting muscle is reduced. This is why a faster rate can reduce the time available for supply.
学校氧供框架有三个锚点：舒张时间、冠脉通畅程度和动脉氧含量。左心室冠脉灌注主要发生在舒张期，此时收缩心肌对血管压迫减轻，因此心率过快会压缩供血时间。

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:41.328
An open vessel is not sufficient if perfusion pressure is poor or oxygen content is inadequate. Oxygen content depends heavily on haemoglobin and saturation. A normal saturation does not establish a normal haemoglobin concentration or guarantee adequate myocardial oxygen delivery.
若灌注压力差或氧含量不足，血管通畅也不够。氧含量高度依赖血红蛋白和饱和度；饱和度正常不能证明血红蛋白正常，也不保证足够心肌供氧。

00:00:41.328 --> 00:01:00.240
Demand reflects how much work the myocardium performs. A faster heart rate means more contractions per minute; stronger contractility and higher afterload can increase work and oxygen use. Interpret these factors together instead of assuming one rate predicts oxygen demand for everyone.
氧需反映心肌做多少功。更快心率意味着每分钟更多次收缩，更强收缩性及更高后负荷也会增加工作和耗氧。应合并解释，不能假定同一心率对所有人都代表相同氧需。

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:18.912
The supply and demand questions complement rhythm naming. Ask whether available coronary flow and oxygen content can meet the work required of this heart now. A patient with coronary disease, anaemia or impaired pumping may tolerate a rhythm poorly even when another patient tolerates it well.
氧供需问题补充节律命名：此刻可用的冠脉血流和氧含量能否满足该心脏的工作？冠脉病、贫血或泵功能受损患者可能难以耐受某节律，而另一患者可良好耐受。

00:01:18.912 --> 00:01:36.216
Sustained tachycardia can simultaneously raise demand and shorten diastolic supply time. It can also impair ventricular filling, reducing stroke volume. This explains why a fast rhythm may become dangerous before the monitor changes to a different named rhythm.
持续心动过速可同时增加氧需、缩短舒张供血时间，也可妨碍心室充盈、降低每搏量。这解释了为何监护仍显示同名节律时，快速节律也可能已经变危险。

00:01:36.216 --> 00:01:56.040
However, tachycardia may be compensating for blood loss, fever or another illness. The mechanism guides the response: address the patient’s condition through the authorized pathway rather than reflexively reducing every fast rate. Determine whether the rhythm is cause, consequence or both.
但心动过速也可能在代偿失血、发热或其他疾病。机制指导行动，应按授权流程处理患者状况，而不是反射性压低所有快速心率；要判断节律是原因、结果，还是两者兼有。

00:01:56.040 --> 00:02:15.000
A slow rate can cause a different problem: even with low demand, cardiac output may be insufficient if stroke volume cannot compensate. Low output can reduce arterial and coronary perfusion pressure. More time between beats is not automatically protective if not enough blood is being delivered.
缓慢心率造成另一种问题：即使氧需低，若每搏量不能代偿，心输出量仍可能不足；低输出又可降低动脉和冠脉灌注压力。若输送的血不够，搏动间隔更长并不自动具有保护作用。

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:34.776
Assess mentation, pulse, skin, pressure trend and symptoms to decide whether the patient is tolerating the rate. Do not use either a bradycardia cutoff or a normal-looking electrical pattern as the entire decision. Important block can deteriorate despite a temporarily adequate pressure reading.
应结合意识、脉搏、皮肤、血压趋势和症状判断是否耐受该频率，不能只凭过缓界值或看似正常的电形态决策。重要阻滞即使暂时血压尚可，也可能恶化。

00:02:34.776 --> 00:02:54.912
Coordinated atrial contraction contributes to late ventricular filling. Losing that coordination in AF or AV dissociation can reduce filling and stroke volume, especially in older or stiff ventricles. The importance is patient-dependent; it is not a fixed percentage to apply to every heart.
协调心房收缩有助于心室舒张晚期充盈。房颤或房室分离时失去协调，可降低充盈和每搏量，尤其在老年或顺应性差的心室中。其重要性因患者而异，不是人人相同的固定百分比。

00:02:54.912 --> 00:03:15.144
Ventricular pacing may restore rate without restoring physiological AV timing. Therefore a paced rate that appears normal still requires assessment of pulse and perfusion. Evaluate the complete supply–demand balance rather than equating a device-generated number with normal cardiovascular function.
心室起搏可能恢复频率，却未恢复生理房室时序。因此，起搏频率看似正常仍需评估脉搏和灌注。应评估完整氧供需平衡，不能把设备给出的数值等同正常心血管功能。

00:03:15.144 --> 00:03:35.136
A prolonged QT chiefly identifies a problem of repolarization vulnerability rather than simply excessive myocardial work. Medication exposure, electrolytes and inherited susceptibility matter. A comfortable patient with normal pressure can still have a concerning repolarization finding.
QT 延长主要提示复极易损性问题，而不只是心肌工作过多。药物、电解质和遗传易感性都重要。患者舒适、血压正常，也可能仍有值得警惕的复极发现。

00:03:35.136 --> 00:03:53.832
Use both frameworks. Ask whether oxygen delivery meets current work, and independently ask whether recovery is electrically vulnerable. State the mechanism and the evidence supporting it, then choose monitoring, communication and escalation consistent with the patient’s condition and your authority.
两种框架都要使用：一方面问供氧是否满足当前工作，另一方面独立问复极是否易损。说明机制与证据，再按患者状况和自身权限选择监护、沟通和升级。
